# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage.json
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ── Node / frontend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.npm-cache/
frontend/dist/
static/spa/

# ── Sphinx ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/_build/
# Where the built HTML is staged for the app to serve. The Docker build writes it from the docs
# stage; a developer running locally writes it with sphinx-build. Either way it is output, and
# committing it would mean the docs a deployment serves could be older than the pages they came
# from -- with nothing to reveal the gap.
static/docs/
# Generated reference pages under docs/reference/ are COMMITTED, deliberately. The drift check
# (`bin/gen-docs-reference.py --check`) diffs the tree against a fresh generation, which it can
# only do if the tree is tracked -- and a schema change showing up as a docs diff in the merge
# request is the review signal that makes the check worth having.

# ── Runtime state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The bind-mounted data directory. Everything durable lives here, which is exactly
# why it must never be committed: it holds assessment artifacts, the SQLite
# database, and the audit trail.
var/
!var/.gitkeep

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/check_no_secrets_in_git.sh fails the lint stage if any of these become
# tracked, because .gitignore only protects files nobody has force-added yet.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
factory.toml
*.pem
*.key
!**/testdata/**/*.key
*.p12
oidc-client-secret*

# ── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
